Why Is It So Hard to Put Down Your Phone?

{{g:Have you ever picked up|현재완료 경험: Have you ever + p.p.? (~해 본 적 있니?)}} your phone {{g:to check|to부정사 부사적 용법(목적): ~하기 위해}} just one message? Then, thirty minutes later, you were still {{v:scrolling}}. You are not alone. Many teenagers {{g:find it hard to stop|가목적어 it + 진목적어 to부정사: ~하는 것이 어렵다고 느끼다}} using their phones. {{t:There is a scientific reason for this.}}

When we get a "like" or a new message, our brain makes a {{v:chemical}} called dopamine. Dopamine {{g:makes us feel good|사역동사 make + 목적어 + 동사원형: ~가 …하게 만들다}}. So our brain wants to have the same feeling again and again. App designers know this very well. That is why many apps have {{v:endless}} scrolling and red {{v:notification}} dots. These things {{g:keep us looking|keep + 목적어 + -ing: ~가 계속 …하게 하다}} at the screen.

Too much phone time can cause some problems. It can make it hard to {{v:fall asleep}}. It can also make it hard to {{v:focus}}. It can even make us feel more {{v:worried}}.

Luckily, there are easy ways to take back {{v:control}}. {{g:Turn off|명령문: 동사원형으로 시작 (~해라)}} notifications for apps you don't need. Keep your phone outside your bedroom at night. You can also set a {{v:daily}} time limit in your phone's settings. {{t:Your phone should be a useful tool. It should not control your life.}}
